From 7d2fa4f1bcc31a52698f4f4d63e2dbe280b6ac55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Christian=20K=C3=BCndig?= <christian@kuendig.info>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 07:26:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] nvapi: Match CUDA devices by PCI location instead of LUID

cuDeviceGetLuid needs CUDA 10, while the applications querying the
CUDA topology (legacy PhysX) predate it and CUDA implementations aimed
at them may not provide it. It is also not a primary identity on Wine:
there the LUID is derived from the device UUID, so it only matches when
the CUDA implementation and the Vulkan driver report the same UUID.

Use the PCI domain, bus and device instead, read through
cuDeviceGetAttribute (available since CUDA 4.0), and compare them with
the adapter's VK_EXT_pci_bus_info properties. This is the identity
already used to find NVML devices. Adapters without PCI bus info are not
matched, and CUDA is not loaded at all when no adapter has it. CUDA
does not report the PCI function, so a device matching several adapters
is ignored as before.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
